## Why This Is Asked

This question probes memory reclamation under contention, cross-service isolation, and CAS-based synchronization in a NUMA-aware kernel, testing both design and practicality.

## Key Concepts

- Per-service quotas in a shared cache
- Deterministic eviction scheduling
- CAS-based victim claims
- Backpressure signaling to avoid thrash
- NUMA-aware replenishment and cross-slab coordination

## Code Example

```c
// Pseudo sketch: CAS-based page claim within a slab
typedef struct { int claimed; } page_t;
typedef struct { page_t *pages; size_t n; } slab_t;
int evict_one(slab_t *s) {
  for (size_t i = 0; i < s->n; i++) {
    if (__sync_bool_compare_and_swap(&s->pages[i].claimed, 0, 1)) {
      // evict this page
      return 1;
    }
  }
  return 0;
}
```

